<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jesús de Cárdenas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jesús de Cárdenas was a Mexican lawyer and federalist politician who was named president of the Republic of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande">Rio Grande</a> in January 1840, when federalist leaders in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamaulipas">Tamaulipas</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuevo-leon">Nuevo León</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coahuila">Coahuila</a> declared independence from the centralist government. The republic existed mainly as a military campaign under Antonio Canales and collapsed by the end of 1840, after which Cárdenas returned to the Mexican government's service.</p></div>
